WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:04.300
Before any team executes a complex play,

00:04.300 --> 00:07.380
they ensure all the elements are in place.

00:07.380 --> 00:11.360
We need to do the same for your 90-day plan.

00:11.360 --> 00:15.160
This pre-game check isn't just about you.

00:15.160 --> 00:17.320
It's about ensuring alignment

00:17.320 --> 00:19.720
and two other critical areas,

00:19.720 --> 00:23.800
your key relationships and your organization.

00:23.800 --> 00:25.520
So let's start there.

00:25.520 --> 00:28.560
We'll look at what's required for you personally,

00:28.560 --> 00:31.800
but we'll also ask how does your plan align

00:31.800 --> 00:36.080
with your team's goals and your organization's priorities?

00:36.080 --> 00:38.580
And do you have the relational alignment

00:38.580 --> 00:41.300
with your manager and stakeholders

00:41.300 --> 00:44.520
and their expectations to make it happen?

00:44.520 --> 00:47.240
Now, don't worry about whether you have

00:47.240 --> 00:49.160
all these pieces in place.

00:49.160 --> 00:53.480
Just think about what's required to succeed.

00:53.480 --> 00:55.160
For this pre-game check,

00:55.200 --> 00:58.560
we will look at the prerequisites in two key areas,

00:58.560 --> 01:00.280
your personal readiness

01:00.280 --> 01:04.040
and your relational organizational alignment.

01:04.040 --> 01:07.160
First, personal readiness.

01:07.160 --> 01:09.560
This is your internal state.

01:09.560 --> 01:11.440
It includes your mindset,

01:11.440 --> 01:14.200
the belief you can achieve your goals,

01:14.200 --> 01:16.760
your motivation and your energy,

01:16.760 --> 01:21.360
your specific skills, knowledge and credentials.

01:21.360 --> 01:23.740
But that's only half of the picture.

01:23.740 --> 01:25.980
The other half is your relational

01:25.980 --> 01:28.020
and organizational alignment.

01:28.020 --> 01:30.860
This is how you show up as a leader.

01:30.860 --> 01:33.540
This includes your manager alignment,

01:33.540 --> 01:37.820
peer collaboration, direct report relationships.

01:37.820 --> 01:40.020
Having both your personal readiness

01:40.020 --> 01:42.060
and your relational alignment in place

01:42.060 --> 01:46.000
is what truly prepares you for the game.

01:46.000 --> 01:47.880
Let me give you an example.

01:47.880 --> 01:52.100
I worked with Lynn, an attorney reentering the workplace

01:52.100 --> 01:55.580
and becoming lead in-house counsel.

01:55.580 --> 01:59.060
Her success wasn't just about her personal skills.

01:59.060 --> 02:03.940
It was about creating a 360 degree alignment.

02:03.940 --> 02:07.300
First, she needed relational alignment at home,

02:07.300 --> 02:09.980
getting on the same page with her spouse

02:09.980 --> 02:12.860
and securing reliable childcare system

02:12.860 --> 02:15.740
to help her in her new schedule.

02:15.740 --> 02:19.640
Then she established manager alignment at work.

02:19.640 --> 02:22.160
She and her new boss created a plan

02:22.160 --> 02:25.080
with crystal clear priorities.

02:25.080 --> 02:29.640
Finally, that clarity cascaded to her new team.

02:29.640 --> 02:32.120
Guided by a shared purpose and mission,

02:32.120 --> 02:37.120
they were all empowered to say no to low impact requests.

02:37.360 --> 02:41.080
This protected their time and focused their energy,

02:41.080 --> 02:44.080
driving incredible efficiency.

02:44.080 --> 02:47.880
That is how alignment across your entire life

02:47.880 --> 02:50.760
creates productivity that you need to handle

02:50.760 --> 02:53.600
major moments of change.

02:53.600 --> 02:55.840
Understanding all of these prerequisites

02:55.840 --> 02:57.560
didn't discourage her.

02:57.560 --> 02:59.120
It empowered her.

02:59.120 --> 03:03.720
It gave her a clear checklist of what she needed to work on.

03:03.720 --> 03:07.080
In your playbook, the first drill will guide you

03:07.080 --> 03:10.880
through identifying the essential elements of success

03:10.880 --> 03:12.480
for your own vision.

03:12.480 --> 03:14.800
This is your pregame check.

